From: abcvicelli <147180743+abcvicelli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] f2fs: take the HPB inode from the pagecache page

f2fs_submit_page_write() took the inode for the Samsung HPB flag from
bio_page->mapping. With fs-layer encryption bio_page is the fscrypt
bounce page, which has no mapping, so the first fdatasync() of an
encrypted file oopses (NULL dereference at f2fs_submit_page_write+0x228,
data.c:1021) and the device bootloops as soon as /data uses FBEv2.

Use fio->page, the pagecache page that is always attached to a mapping,
like the f2fs_crypt_mergeable_bio()/f2fs_set_bio_crypt_ctx() calls in the
same function.

---
diff --git a/fs/f2fs/data.c b/fs/f2fs/data.c
index 724791c13..81ac7efb1 100644
--- a/fs/f2fs/data.c
+++ b/fs/f2fs/data.c
@@ -1018,7 +1018,7 @@ void f2fs_submit_page_write(struct f2fs_io_info *fio)
 	else
 		bio_page = fio->page;
 
-	inode = bio_page->mapping->host;
+	inode = fio->page->mapping->host;
 
 	/* set submitted = true as a return value */
 	fio->submitted = true;
